exercises.solution:
```python
def members(x):
    return [y for y in range(x.bit_length()) if x >> y & 1]


def rank(x):
    return max((rank(y) + 1 for y in members(x)), default=0)
```

Every member $y$ of $x$ satisfies $y \lt x$ (since $2^y \le x$), so the recursion is well-founded — a finite shadow of $\in$-induction. The tests check that sampled codes below $65536 = |V_5|$ have rank at most $4$, i.e. lie in $V_5$, and that $65536 = 2^{16}$, the code of $\{16\}$, has rank $5$.
